.TH TELEGRAM-NOTIFY 1 "2026-09-15" "telegram-notifier 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
telegram\-notify \- send a notification to Telegram
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B telegram\-notify
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ TEXT .\|.\|.]
.br
.B telegram\-notify
.B \-\-ping
|
.B \-\-status
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B telegram\-notify
hands a message to the
.BR telegram\-notifierd (8)
daemon, which queues it and delivers it to Telegram. The command returns as
soon as the daemon has written the message to its persistent queue, not when
Telegram has accepted it; delivery, retries and rate limiting happen in the
background.
.PP
If no
.I TEXT
operand is given, the message body is read from standard input.
.PP
Sending requires write access to the daemon's control socket, which is owned
by the
.B telegram\-notify
group. Add users to that group with
.BR adduser (8).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-target " " \fINAME\fR
Send to the named target from the daemon's configuration instead of the
configured default. Use
.B \-\-status
to list the available targets.
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-title " " \fITEXT\fR
Heading placed above the body. It is emphasised and escaped according to the
selected format.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-priority " " \fILEVEL\fR
One of
.BR low ", " normal " (default) or " high .
Higher priorities leave the queue first, which matters when a backlog has
built up.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " " \fIFORMAT\fR
Body markup:
.BR plain ", " markdown ", " markdownv2 " or " html .
Defaults to the target's configured format. With anything other than
.BR plain ,
escaping reserved characters is the caller's responsibility; Telegram rejects
malformed markup and the message is then moved to the failed queue.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-silent
Deliver without a notification sound.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-source " " \fINAME\fR
Label recorded in the daemon's log for this message. Defaults to the systemd
unit or the invoking user.
.TP
.B \-\-stdin
Read the body from standard input even when
.I TEXT
operands are present; the operands then become the first line.
.TP
.B \-\-socket " " \fIPATH\fR
Control socket to connect to. Defaults to
.I /run/telegram\-notifier/notifier.sock
and may also be set with
.BR TELEGRAM_NOTIFIER_SOCKET .
.TP
.B \-\-timeout " " \fISECONDS\fR
How long to wait for the daemon to answer. Default 10.
.TP
.B \-\-ping
Check that the daemon is reachable and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-status
Print queue statistics and the configured targets as JSON, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Do not print the queued message id on success.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help ", " \-V ", " \-\-version
Show help or version information.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The message was queued, or the ping or status request succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
The daemon rejected the request, for instance because the target is unknown
or the queue is full.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error, or the daemon could not be reached.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TELEGRAM_NOTIFIER_SOCKET
Overrides the default control socket path.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Send a one line message to the default target:
.PP
.RS
.EX
telegram\-notify "Backup finished"
.EE
.RE
.PP
Send the tail of a log to the ops chat, as an urgent message:
.PP
.RS
.EX
journalctl \-u nginx \-n 20 | telegram\-notify \-t ops \-p high \\
    \-\-title "nginx restarted" \-\-stdin
.EE
.RE
.PP
Use it as a cron failure handler, without letting it break the job:
.PP
.RS
.EX
0 3 * * * /usr/local/bin/backup || telegram\-notify \-p high "backup failed"
.EE
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/telegram-notifier/notifier.sock
Default control socket.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR telegram\-notifierd (8),
.BR telegram\-notifier.toml (5)
